{
  "_id": "6afcde8c69eab6fdff2d8b44",
  "Package": "dagLogo",
  "Type": "Package",
  "Title": "dagLogo: a Bioconductor package for visualizing conserved amino\nacid sequence pattern in groups based on probability theory",
  "Version": "1.51.1",
  "Authors@R": "c(person(given=\"Jianhong\", family=\"Ou\", email=\"jou@morgridge.org\", \nrole=c(\"aut\", \"cre\"), comment=c(ORCID=\"0000-0002-8652-2488\")),\nperson(given=\"Haibo\", family=\"Liu\", role=\"aut\"),\nperson(given=\"Alexey\", family=\"Stukalov\", role=\"ctr\"),\nperson(given=\"Niraj\", family=\"Nirala\", role=\"ctr\"),\nperson(given=\"Usha\", family=\"Acharya\", role=\"ctr\"),\nperson(given=\"Julie Lihua\", family=\"Zhu\",\nrole=\"aut\", email=\"Julie.Zhu@umassmed.edu\"))",
  "Description": "Visualize significant conserved amino acid sequence\npattern in groups based on probability theory. The package\nallows aligned or not aligned subsequences of different length\nas input. Both significantly over- and under-represented amino\nacid residues can be plotted. AA residues can be grouped and\nstatistical significance test can be performed at the group\nlevel.",
